<title>MEXICO: Mexico to launch nearly $1 bln tourist development.</title>
<headline>Mexico to launch nearly $1 bln tourist development.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A new tourist development that cost $937 million will be launched on Saturday in the western Pacific resort of Manzanillo, Colima state, the developer Turbana said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said the site would be called Hotel Gran Bay, run by the U.S. chain Carnival Hotels and Casinos, and would include a golf course, two marinas and a yacht club aimed chiefly at foreign tourism.</p>
<p>Turbana said President Ernesto Zedillo would open it.</p>
<p>-- Monica Ballesca, Guadalajara newsroom +523 817-0397</p>
